.Dd April 6, 2026
.Dt DOCGAP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm docgap
.Nd FreeBSD Documentation Gap Detector \(em monitors commits and generates documentation patches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar config_file
.Op Fl v
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm run
.Op Fl s Ar timestamp
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm status
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm log
.Op Fl -since Ar date
.Op Fl -status Ar status
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm init
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm report
.Op Fl -format Ar txt Ns | Ns Ar json
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm config Cm show
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm review Cm list
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm review Cm show
.Ar commit_hash
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm review Cm approve
.Op Ar commit_hash
.Op Fl -all
.Op Fl -since Ar timestamp
.Op Fl -reviewer Ar name
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm review Cm reject
.Ar commit_hash
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Op Fl -reviewer Ar name
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm reprocess
.Op Ar commit_hash
.Op Fl -failed
.Op Fl -pending
.Op Fl -stage1 Ar hash
.Op Fl -stage2 Ar hash
.Op Fl -since Ar timestamp
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -max-retries Ar n
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm heal
.Op Fl -fix
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm validate
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm reset
.Ar commit_hash
.Op Fl -confirm
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm purge
.Fl -before Ar timestamp
.Op Fl -status Ar status
.Op Fl -include-output
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -confirm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a batch-processing pipeline that monitors FreeBSD source commits and generates
documentation patches using local LLM inference.
.Pp
The tool operates in two sequential stages:
.Bl -tag -width "Stage 2"
.It Stage 1
.Em Detection :
classifies each new commit as
.Sy needs_doc ,
.Sy irrelevant ,
or
.Sy uncertain
using a locally-running LLM model via Ollama.
.It Stage 2
.Em Generation :
produces draft documentation patches in mdoc(7) or AsciiDoc format for
commits that were classified as requiring documentation.
.El
.Pp
Results are stored in a SQLite database and an output directory.
Human reviewers then inspect the generated patches and mark commits as
.Sy reviewed
(approved) or
.Sy false_positive
(no documentation needed).
.Sh COMMIT STATE MACHINE
Each commit tracked by
.Nm
transitions through the following states:
.Bl -tag -width "false_positive"
.It Sy pending
Commit has been fetched but not yet classified.
.It Sy needs_doc
Stage\~1 classified the commit as requiring documentation.
.It Sy doc_generated
Stage\~2 has produced a draft patch for the commit.
.It Sy uncertain
Stage\~1 could not reach a confident classification.
.It Sy irrelevant
Stage\~1 determined no documentation change is needed.
.It Sy reviewed
A reviewer approved the commit (via
.Cm review approve ) .
.It Sy false_positive
A reviewer rejected the commit (via
.Cm review reject ) .
.It Sy submitted
The documentation patch has been submitted upstream.
.It Sy error
Stage\~1 classification encountered an unrecoverable error.
Can be retried via
.Cm reprocess .
.It Sy generation_error
Stage\~2 generation failed.
Can be retried via
.Cm reprocess .
.El
.Pp
Valid transitions:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pending --> needs_doc | irrelevant | uncertain  (Stage 1)
needs_doc --> doc_generated                     (Stage 2)
needs_doc | doc_generated --> reviewed          (approve)
needs_doc | doc_generated | uncertain --> false_positive  (reject)
pending --> error                              (Stage 1 failure)
needs_doc --> generation_error                 (Stage 2 failure)
error | generation_error --> pending           (reset or reprocess)
.Ed
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss docgap run
Execute the full detection and generation pipeline.
Fetches new commits from the configured repositories, runs Stage\~1 classification
on pending commits, and runs Stage\~2 generation on commits classified as
.Sy needs_doc .
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl s Ar timestamp , Fl -since Ar timestamp
Process only commits authored on or after the given ISO 8601 timestamp
(e.g.,
.Dq 2026-04-01T00:00:00Z ) .
Useful for backfilling a specific time range.
.It Fl -dry-run
Run classification and generation without writing any results to the database.
Useful for testing LLM responses or verifying pipeline behaviour.
.El
.Ss docgap status
Show system status and pipeline health.
Displays the last successful run, per-status commit counts, the output
directory file count, and LLM connectivity.
Requires the database to be initialized (see
.Cm init ) .
.Ss docgap log
Query analyzed commits stored in the database.
By default, shows commits with status
.Sy pending
or
.Sy needs_doc .
Output is limited to the 50 most recent matching commits.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -since Ar date
Show only commits whose recorded date is on or after
.Ar date
(ISO 8601 format).
.It Fl -status Ar status
Filter results to commits with the given status.
Valid values:
.Sy pending ,
.Sy needs_doc ,
.Sy doc_generated ,
.Sy irrelevant ,
.Sy uncertain ,
.Sy reviewed ,
.Sy false_positive ,
.Sy submitted .
.El
.Ss docgap init
Initialize the SQLite database and required output directories under the
configured
.Va data_dir .
Safe to run multiple times; existing data is not overwritten.
Creates the following subdirectories:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa <data_dir>/output/
.It
.Pa <data_dir>/repos/
.El
.Ss docgap report
Generate a detailed documentation report covering all actionable commits.
The report includes commit statistics, last run information, and detailed
listings for commits needing documentation, commits with generated docs,
uncertain commits requiring triage, and error commits.
.Pp
Data is gathered from both the SQLite database (commit metadata,
classifications, and run history) and the output directory (generated
file listings and report previews from
.Pa report.txt ) .
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -format Ar fmt
Output format.
.Ar fmt
may be
.Cm txt
(human-readable with section headers, default) or
.Cm json
(structured data with full commit details for scripting).
.It Fl -output Ar path
Save the report to the specified file path.
The report is also printed to standard output.
.It Fl -save
Save the report to the
.Pa reports/
subdirectory under
.Va data_dir
with a timestamped filename
(e.g.,
.Pa report-20260406-140000.txt ) .
The report is also printed to standard output.
.El
.Pp
The text report organizes commits into sections:
.Bl -tag -width "DOCUMENTATION GENERATED" -compact
.It Sy NEEDS DOCUMENTATION
Commits classified as requiring documentation but not yet generated.
Shows hash, subject, author, category, confidence, doc target, and reasoning.
.It Sy DOCUMENTATION GENERATED
Commits with generated patches ready for review.
Includes output file listing and a preview of the generated report.
.It Sy UNCERTAIN
Commits the LLM could not confidently classify, requiring human triage.
.It Sy ERRORS
Commits that encountered processing errors, with retry count and error details.
.El
.Ss docgap config show
Display the active configuration, including all sections and their resolved
values as loaded from the configuration file.
Useful for confirming that overrides via
.Fl -config
or
.Ev DOCGAP_CONFIG
are being applied correctly.
.Ss docgap review
Manage human review of flagged commits.
.Cm review
is a command group with the following subcommands:
.Bl -tag -width "approve"
.It Cm list
List commits that are awaiting review.
Shows commits with status
.Sy needs_doc
or
.Sy doc_generated ,
including their LLM classification, confidence score, and category.
Output is limited to 20 entries.
.It Cm show Ar commit_hash
Display full review details for the commit identified by
.Ar commit_hash .
Shows classification metadata, LLM reasoning, and the content of any
generated report or patch files stored in the output directory.
.It Cm approve Op Ar commit_hash Op Fl -all Op Fl -since Ar timestamp Op Fl -reviewer Ar name
Mark one or more commits as approved for documentation update, transitioning
their status from
.Sy needs_doc
or
.Sy doc_generated
to
.Sy reviewed .
.Pp
When
.Ar commit_hash
is given, only that single commit is approved.
With
.Fl -all ,
all approvable commits are approved in bulk, optionally restricted to those
added on or after
.Fl -since Ar timestamp .
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ar commit_hash
Hash of the specific commit to approve.
.It Fl -all
Approve all commits currently in an approvable state
.Pq Sy needs_doc No or Sy doc_generated .
.It Fl -since Ar timestamp
When used with
.Fl -all ,
limit bulk approval to commits on or after this ISO 8601 timestamp.
.It Fl -reviewer Ar name
Record
.Ar name
as the reviewer.
Defaults to the value of
.Ev USER .
.El
.It Cm reject Ar commit_hash Op Fl -reason Ar text Op Fl -reviewer Ar name
Mark a commit as a false positive \(em no documentation is needed.
Transitions the commit status from
.Sy needs_doc ,
.Sy doc_generated ,
or
.Sy uncertain
to
.Sy false_positive .
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ar commit_hash
Hash of the commit to reject.
.It Fl r Ar text , Fl -reason Ar text
Free-text reason for the rejection, stored as reviewer feedback.
.It Fl -reviewer Ar name
Record
.Ar name
as the reviewer.
Defaults to the value of
.Ev USER .
.El
.El
.Ss docgap reprocess
Reprocess failed or incomplete commits through the pipeline.
Retries commits that were interrupted or encountered errors during
Stage\~1 detection or Stage\~2 generation.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ar commit_hash
Reprocess a specific commit through both stages.
.It Fl -failed
Reprocess all commits with
.Sy error
or
.Sy generation_error
status.
.It Fl -pending
Reprocess all commits with
.Sy needs_doc
status that have not yet generated documentation.
.It Fl -stage1 Ar hash
Re-run only Stage\~1 (detection) for the specified commit.
.It Fl -stage2 Ar hash
Re-run only Stage\~2 (generation) for the specified commit.
Requires the commit to have
.Sy needs_doc
classification.
.It Fl -since Ar timestamp
Reprocess all commits since the given ISO 8601 timestamp.
.It Fl -dry-run
Show what would be reprocessed without writing changes.
.It Fl -max-retries Ar n
Maximum retry count per commit before skipping (default: 3).
Prevents infinite retry loops.
.El
.Ss docgap heal
Detect and repair interrupted runs and stuck commits.
Without
.Fl -fix ,
reports issues found without making changes.
.Pp
Checks performed:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Stale runs (status
.Sy running
for more than 24 hours)
.It
Incomplete Stage\~2 (commits with
.Sy needs_doc
but no output files)
.It
Retryable errors (commits with
.Sy error
or
.Sy generation_error
below the retry limit)
.El
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -fix
Automatically repair detected issues: mark stale runs as failed and
reprocess stuck commits.
.It Fl -dry-run
Show what
.Fl -fix
would do without writing changes.
.El
.Ss docgap validate
Check system integrity.
Verifies configuration, database connectivity, repository state,
LLM server health, and data directory permissions.
.Pp
Exit codes:
.Bl -tag -width "2" -compact
.It 0
All checks passed.
.It 1
One or more warnings (non-critical).
.It 2
One or more errors (critical).
.El
.Ss docgap reset
Reset a commit to
.Sy pending
status for full reprocessing.
Clears the commit's classification, confidence, category, and reasoning,
increments the retry counter, and removes any output directory.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ar commit_hash
Hash of the commit to reset.
.It Fl -confirm
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt.
.El
.Ss docgap purge
Clean old data from the database and optionally remove output directories.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -before Ar timestamp
.Pq required
Purge commits older than this ISO 8601 timestamp.
.It Fl -status Ar status
Restrict purge to commits with this status.
May be repeated for multiple statuses.
Default: only terminal statuses
.Pq Sy irrelevant , false_positive , reviewed , submitted .
.It Fl -include-output
Also delete output directories for purged commits.
.It Fl -dry-run
Show what would be purged without making changes.
.It Fl -confirm
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Global Options
The following options apply to all commands and must be given before the
command name.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Path to the YAML configuration file.
Overrides the
.Ev DOCGAP_CONFIG
environment variable.
Default:
.Pa config/config.yaml .
On a production FreeBSD installation the default is typically
.Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/config.yaml .
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Enable verbose (DEBUG-level) log output.
Without this flag, only INFO-level and above messages are printed.
.It Fl -version
Print the
.Nm
version string and exit.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads its configuration from a YAML file.
The file path is resolved in the following order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
The
.Fl -config
command-line option.
.It
The
.Ev DOCGAP_CONFIG
environment variable.
.It
The compiled-in default path.
.El
.Pp
Run
.Nm Cm config Cm show
to print all resolved configuration values.
.Pp
The configuration file is organized into sections:
.Bl -tag -width "repositories"
.It Sy general
.Bl -tag -width "log_level" -compact
.It Va data_dir
Root directory for the database, output files, and cloned repositories.
.It Va log_level
Logging verbosity (e.g.,
.Dq INFO ,
.Dq DEBUG ) .
.El
.It Sy repositories
.Bl -tag -width "freebsd_src.remote" -compact
.It Va freebsd_src.path
Local path for the FreeBSD
.Pa src
repository checkout.
.It Va freebsd_src.remote
Upstream URL used to fetch new commits.
.It Va freebsd_doc.path
Local path for the FreeBSD
.Pa doc
repository checkout.
.It Va freebsd_doc.remote
Upstream URL for the documentation repository.
.El
.It Sy llm
.Bl -tag -width "timeout" -compact
.It Va base_url
HTTP base URL for the Ollama API (e.g.,
.Dq http://localhost:11434 ) .
.It Va model
Ollama model name to use for inference.
.It Va timeout
Request timeout in seconds.
.El
.It Sy detection
.Bl -tag -width "confidence_threshold_reject" -compact
.It Va confidence_threshold_accept
Minimum confidence score (0\(en1) to classify a commit as
.Sy needs_doc .
.It Va confidence_threshold_reject
Maximum confidence score to classify a commit as
.Sy irrelevant .
Commits between the two thresholds are marked
.Sy uncertain .
.El
.It Sy generation
.Bl -tag -width "validate_asciidoc" -compact
.It Va validate_mdoc
If
.Dq true ,
validate generated mdoc(7) patches with
.Xr mandoc 1 .
.It Va validate_asciidoc
If
.Dq true ,
validate generated AsciiDoc patches.
.El
.It Sy notification
.Bl -tag -width "committer_notify" -compact
.It Va doceng_recipients
List of email addresses that receive documentation-gap digests.
.It Va committer_notify
If
.Dq true ,
also notify the original commit author.
.It Va from_address
Envelope sender address for outgoing notifications.
.El
.It Sy debug
.Bl -tag -width "include_config_snapshot" -compact
.It Va llm_logging
If
.Dq true ,
save all LLM prompts and responses to disk under
.Pa <data_dir>/debug/<commit-hash>/ .
Useful for cross-model performance evaluation.
Default:
.Dq false .
.It Va log_dir
Directory for debug log output.
Defaults to
.Pa <data_dir>/debug .
.It Va max_debug_entries
Maximum number of debug directories to retain before rotating oldest.
Default: 500.
.It Va include_config_snapshot
If
.Dq true ,
include detection and generation settings in
.Pa metadata.json .
Default:
.Dq true .
.El
.El
.Sh PROMPT TEMPLATES
.Nm
uses LLM prompt templates for both Stage\~1 classification and Stage\~2
generation.
Templates are loaded using a three-level fallback chain:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/prompts/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .txt
\(em system override (highest priority).
.It
.Pa prompts/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .txt
relative to the installation directory \(em project-level override.
.It
Hardcoded default embedded in the Python source \(em always available.
.El
.Pp
The
.Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/prompts/
directory is created empty during installation.
This is by design: the built-in defaults work without any template files.
To customize a prompt, create a file with the appropriate name:
.Bl -tag -width "generation-asciidoc.txt"
.It Pa detection.txt
Stage\~1 classification prompt.
.It Pa generation-mdoc.txt
Stage\~2 prompt for mdoc(7) manpage generation.
.It Pa generation-asciidoc.txt
Stage\~2 prompt for AsciiDoc handbook/article generation.
.El
.Pp
System-level files in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/prompts/
take precedence over project-level files and built-in defaults.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DOCGAP_CONFIG"
.It Ev DOCGAP_CONFIG
Path to the YAML configuration file.
Overridden by the
.Fl -config
option.
.It Ev USER
Login name of the current user.
Used as the default
.Fl -reviewer
name when approving or rejecting commits.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Ss Data Files
.Bl -tag -width "/var/db/docgap/output/<hash>/handbook.patch"
.It Pa <data_dir>/docgap.sqlite
SQLite database storing commit records, pipeline run history, and
notification state.
.It Pa <data_dir>/output/
Root directory for all generated artifacts.
.It Pa <data_dir>/output/ Ns Ar hash Ns Pa /report.txt
Human-readable analysis report for a specific commit.
.It Pa <data_dir>/output/ Ns Ar hash Ns Pa /manpage.patch
Generated mdoc(7) patch for commits targeting manual pages.
.It Pa <data_dir>/output/ Ns Ar hash Ns Pa /handbook.patch
Generated AsciiDoc patch for commits targeting the FreeBSD Handbook or other book/article content.
.It Pa <data_dir>/repos/
Directory where repository checkouts are managed.
.It Pa <data_dir>/debug/
Root directory for LLM debug logs (when
.Va debug.llm_logging
is enabled).
.It Pa <data_dir>/debug/ Ns Ar hash Ns Pa /metadata.json
Model information, timestamps, and configuration snapshot for a commit.
.El
.Ss Configuration Files
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/docgap/config.yaml"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/config.yaml
Primary configuration file for production FreeBSD installations.
.It Pa config/config.yaml.sample
Annotated sample configuration file distributed with the source.
.El
.Ss Service Files
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/rc.d/docgap"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/docgap
FreeBSD rc.d service script for daemon-mode operation.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/cron.d/docgap
Sample cron entry for automated periodic runs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Bl -tag -width "2"
.It 0
Success \(em the command completed without errors.
.It 1
Partial success or a non-fatal error
(e.g., a single commit could not be processed, or a requested
commit hash was not found).
.It 2
Fatal error \(em the pipeline failed to run (e.g., database missing,
configuration invalid).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Initialize the system
Run once after installation before any other command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap init
.Ed
.Ss Run the full pipeline
Fetch new commits and process them through both stages:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap run
.Ed
.Ss Backfill from a specific date
Process all commits since a given timestamp:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap run --since 2026-04-01T00:00:00Z
.Ed
.Ss Dry-run to preview LLM output without writing to the database
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap run --dry-run
.Ed
.Ss Check system health and LLM connectivity
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap status
.Ed
.Ss List commits awaiting review
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap review list
.Ed
.Ss Inspect a specific commit and its generated patch
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap review show abc123def456
.Ed
.Ss Approve a single commit for documentation
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap review approve abc123def456 --reviewer jdoe
.Ed
.Ss Bulk-approve all commits generated since a date
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap review approve --all --since 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z --reviewer jdoe
.Ed
.Ss Reject a commit as a false positive with a reason
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap review reject abc123def456 --reason "Only changes test harness, no public API impact"
.Ed
.Ss Filter the log to commits needing documentation
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap log --status needs_doc
.Ed
.Ss Show commits since a specific date
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap log --since 2026-03-15T00:00:00Z
.Ed
.Ss Print the active configuration
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap config show
.Ed
.Ss Use a custom configuration file
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap --config /etc/myconfig.yaml status
.Ed
.Ss Generate a detailed report
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap report
.Ed
.Ss Save report to the reports directory
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap report --save
.Ed
.Ss Generate a JSON report for monitoring scripts
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap report --format json --output /tmp/docgap-report.json
.Ed
.Ss Cron setup for automated runs
Add to
.Pa /etc/crontab
to run the pipeline every six hours:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
0 */6 * * *  root  /usr/local/bin/docgap run >> /var/db/docgap/logs/cron.log 2>&1
.Ed
.Ss Reprocess all failed commits
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap reprocess --failed
.Ed
.Ss Reprocess only Stage 2 for a specific commit
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap reprocess --stage2 abc123def456
.Ed
.Ss Detect and auto-fix pipeline issues
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap heal --fix
.Ed
.Ss Check system integrity
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap validate
.Ed
.Ss Reset a commit for full reprocessing
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap reset abc123def456 --confirm
.Ed
.Ss Purge old data
.Bd -literal -offset indent
docgap purge --before 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z --include-output --confirm
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -tag -width "LLM connection failed"
.It Database not initialized
The SQLite database does not exist at the configured path.
Run
.Nm Cm init
to create it.
.It LLM connection failed
.Nm
could not reach the Ollama API.
Verify that Ollama is running and the required model is loaded:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ollama ps
ollama pull <model>
.Ed
.It Permission denied
The process lacks write access to
.Va data_dir
or its subdirectories.
Check ownership and permissions.
.It Cannot approve/reject: status is '...'
The commit is in a state that does not permit the requested action.
Consult the state machine in
.Sx COMMIT STATE MACHINE
for valid transitions.
.El
.Sh IMPLICIT BEHAVIORS
The following behaviors occur automatically and may affect operation:
.Ss Pipeline Resume
On its first run with no prior history,
.Nm
processes commits from the last 7 days.
On subsequent runs, it resumes from the
.Va finished_at
timestamp of the last successful run.
Commits already recorded in the database are skipped silently.
.Ss Error Recovery
If the LLM call fails during Stage\~1 classification, the commit is
marked as
.Sy UNCERTAIN
with confidence 0.0 rather than failing the pipeline.
This keeps batch processing running but may mask connectivity issues.
.Ss Input Truncation
Large inputs are truncated automatically to prevent resource exhaustion:
.Bl -tag -width "Commit diff" -compact
.It Commit diff
100,000 characters
.It Commit subject
1,000 characters
.It File list
500 files
.It Doc content
50,000 characters
.It LLM response
200,000 characters
.El
.Pp
Classification and generation are performed on the truncated input.
For very large commits, this may reduce accuracy.
.Ss Placeholder Patches
If Stage\~2 generation produces no valid unified diff, a placeholder
comment with
.Dq TODO: Add documentation here
is saved and the commit is marked
.Sy doc_generated .
Review these outputs carefully.
.Ss Database Initialization
.Cm init
deletes and recreates the database if one already exists.
Back up the database before running
.Cm init
on a system with existing data.
.Ss Configuration File Search
When no
.Fl -config
option is given, the configuration file is searched in order:
.Pa /usr/local/etc/docgap/config.yaml ,
.Pa /etc/docgap/config.yaml ,
then
.Pa config/config.yaml
relative to the installation.
The first file found is used.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr ollama 1 ,
.Xr sqlite3 1 ,
.Xr crontab 5 ,
.Xr mdoc 7 ,
.Xr sendmail 8
